<title>GERMANY: S&amp;P gives &quot;AAA&quot; rating to Munich Re.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P gives &quot;AAA&quot; rating to Munich Re.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. ratings agency Standard &amp; Poor's said on Wednesday that it has rated German reinsurance giant Munich Re and its unit American Re at &quot;AAA&quot;.</p>
<p>This is the highest rating the U.S. agency gives.  </p>
<p>S&amp;P's said it reviewed its rating of Munich Re and reaffirmed its highest rating for the Munich-based group. American Re has been raised to &quot;AAA&quot; from &quot;AA&quot; after the merger with Munich Re was completed.</p>
<p>Munich Re management board chairman Hans-Juergen Schinzler said he was pleased with the rating.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
